+# Flight 93 passenger-list descriptions and missing attachments
+
+November 14, 2026 UTC · TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1. A newly acquired public Commission-release packet contains a September 13 FBI interview with a United Airlines reservation employee and another copy of the September 12 boarding-pass report. The first report describes how the employee read passenger-list entries and identifies a manifest and two passenger-name records as attachments. **Those attachments do not appear in the four physical pages acquired in this packet.** This is additional source evidence for the [previously preserved 38-pass / 37-passenger observations](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/069e2fbe6fe018122d1fab4cc76f600e44820ca5/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-glick-airline-booking-2026-11-14/README.md), not a completed reconciliation.
+
+## Separate observations
+
+| Source and locator | What the record reports |
+| --- | --- |
+| **FBI 302-727**, four-page packet physical p. 1, lines 17–27 | A United reservations employee is described as having a Flight 93 passenger list, also called a manifest, and says she assisted an agent with passenger-name-record information on September 11. The text says a copy of the list is attached. |
+| **Same report**, p. 1 lines 29–35 and p. 2 lines 15–18 | The employee describes two entries with the surname **Britton** as one passenger and an **extra seat**. The continuation says a related passenger-name record is attached. |
+| **Same report**, p. 2 lines 19–30 | The report says a passenger-name record for **Bingham** is attached. It attributes to the employee a separate account of a **double listing for Bingham**, an apparent total of **38**, and a stated total of **37 passengers** including **36 paying passengers plus Bingham**. The source gives these descriptions; the listed manifest and PNRs are needed to test their relationship to each other and to the boarding-pass report. |
+| **FBI NK-744 / item 415**, prior two-page copy pp. 1–2 and this packet pp. 3–4 | The typed report says **38 boarding passes** were supplied for Flight 93 and separately describes **40 ticket coupons and discarded ticket parts from various flights**. The earlier scan bears handwritten marks, including a crossed-out typed entry; the newly acquired scan does not show those marks. The authorship, date and significance of the markings are unverified. [Prior report and exact archive locator](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/069e2fbe6fe018122d1fab4cc76f600e44820ca5/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-glick-airline-booking-2026-11-14/README.md) |
+| **Item 407**, physical p. 1 | A separate FBI document, production header dated **10/29/2002**, describes a review of a flight manifest and lists passengers; handwritten call-related annotations also appear. Its relationship to the manifest and PNRs described as attached to 302-727 is not established. The item does not by itself supply the cited reservation attachments. |
+| [NPS Flight 93 timeline](https://www.nps.gov/flni/learn/historyculture/september-11-2001-timeline.htm) | The introductory summary gives **37 passengers and 7 crew**. Its account is retrospective and not the airline manifest. |
+
+The **38 boarding passes**, the employee's description of an apparent **38** and actual **37**, and the NPS **37 passengers** remain observations from separate records. The new interview supplies a reported explanation that warrants testing, but the different source populations, the separate Britton and Bingham entry descriptions, the underlying rows, and the relationship between the boarding passes and the employee's list remain unverified. Do not select a controlling number or infer an additional passenger, an intentional alteration, or an innocent transcription error from this comparison.
+
+## Source-specific field meanings
+
+In 302-727 p. 1 lines 38–48, the employee explains list markings: the first asterisk indicates check-in, a second indicates collection of a boarding pass by a gate machine, and **ET** is described as an electronic ticket. Those are meanings attributed to this employee for the particular list. The list itself and the audit trail behind each field were not acquired; these definitions are not universal proof that a named person boarded or of what a network time field means.
+
+## Itinerary and custody limits
+
+The new packet contains the employee interview and another NK-744 scan. It does not provide the claimed underlying PNR for the itinerary investigated in the [6390 comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a9b917df176d022ab2b19b7fb785ceddd1bffd4b/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-glick-6390-first-report-2026-11-14/README.md). The 6390 **Cincinnati** wording and 11722 **non-stop** wording remain distinct and unresolved. The separately described **40 mixed-flight coupons** are not established to include any particular passenger or September 10 trip.
+
+- [ ] Locate the manifest and two PNR attachments expressly identified in **302-727**, and obtain version, production and redaction history. Test row counts, entry definitions and the two reported listing descriptions against the actual records before drawing a conclusion.
+- [ ] Obtain the actual NK-744 passes and mixed-flight coupon inventory, chain of custody and disposition; trace any relevant reservation and rebooking records by item, not by the aggregate counts.
+- [ ] Obtain 6390's original notes, source relay and any corrections, as well as independent airline-operation and flight records. No actual itinerary or intentional conduct is established here.
+
+## Acquisition and verification
+
+Two separately indexed members of the [January 2009 Commission ZIP mirror](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip) were acquired by bounded byte ranges with member-name, ETag, length and CRC checks: the four-page employee-interview packet, SHA-256 `55886ea0f19070142de70456b3f343507cf121da327fb17927eaafe4b2b2e1ec`, and the two-page item 407, SHA-256 `f15514f3d4dd3f0deb3a62f8dd22b50b4fb4589018b01f95bbbdccf59a4872ab`. Both copies of NK-744 are reproductions of one report, not independent witnesses. All four packet pages and both item 407 pages were visually screened; selected text anchors and source hashes were checked. Textual differences and markings do not establish a chain of annotations, original-master authenticity or passenger-level truth. Raw passenger records and other personal information remain outside this public derivative. [Exact member paths, byte ranges and source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json).
